    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annōtĭnus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		from annus, as diutinus from diu, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a year old</i>, <i>of last
				year</i> (only in prose and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum annotinis (navibus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 5, 8</span></i>
			 (the paraphrast: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συν ταῖς τοῦ
				πρόσθεν ἔτους</span>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ungues,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 24, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">novus fructus cum annotino,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 26, 44, § 107</span></i>
			.</div>
